    "steps": {
      "site": {
        "title": "The site at a computer's width",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "prose",
            "text": "The Moonlit wheat palette (wheat #ffefae on night #12354e), lockup D (the bare wheat beside \"First the Blade\" in small capitals), the series marks in fine lines on wheat tiles, and N2 \"The sky turns\": the field fades into the paper, series rows parted by hairlines, \"Why we make these\" warms into the wheat, the dusk holds Mark 4:27, and the moonlit night rises with the stacked lockup and the sign-up. No torn paper, tilted card, shadow or disc. The copy is unchanged.\n\nWhere it differs from the round 2 prototype: Mark 4:28's reference and the page labels on the painted sky are in the night ink (the deep wheat fails contrast there); the darker wheat for labels and \"the\" is #7a6813 (the prototype's #a3842a fails contrast on the paper); The Path of the Just's row shows its fine-line mark, not the robe still (the still would claim a film that is not out); the moonlit night's sky is repainted from violet to the night's blue."
          },
